CWhisper: the whisper.cpp speech recognition library in Dirigible

Source: whisper.cpp v1.9.5 (ggml 0.26.0),
https://codeload.github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp/tar.gz/refs/tags/v1.9.5
SHA-256 of the tarball: ff1a9053feb509ff9d7729703355541ae9690073a6b1c40eb692c962e0dc1720
License: MIT. The text is in LICENSE and in Support/Resources/whisper.cpp-LICENSE.txt.

What this folder holds:
- The files of a CPU build with Accelerate BLAS: src/whisper.cpp, src/whisper-arch.h,
  src/aneforge/ (excluded from the target: its header stays for the types of whisper.cpp), the
  ggml core of ggml/src, ggml/src/ggml-cpu (with amx/, tiled/, and arch/x86 and arch/arm),
  ggml/src/ggml-blas, and the public headers of include/ and ggml/include in include/.
- Files from Dirigible, not from whisper.cpp:
  - ggml/src/ggml-version.h: the version defines that CMake makes.
  - include/module.modulemap: the module CWhisper, with whisper.h and cwhisper_stop.h.
  - ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch-x86-quants.c, arch-x86-repack.cpp, arch-arm-quants.c, and
    arch-arm-repack.cpp: each includes one arch file under its arch macro, because the x86 and
    arm files define the same symbols. The arch folder is excluded from the target.
  - cwhisper_stop.c and include/cwhisper_stop.h: the stop flag of one transcription, one
    atomic_bool, and the abort callback of whisper_full that reads it.
  - This file.

Changed files. Each has a dated notice line at its top.

1. Casts (530 -Wshorten-64-to-32 sites, which the XCBuild build of scripts/bundle.sh gives).
   Each cast wraps the whole converted expression in its target type, under the invariant of
   its group. No group needs a type change.
   Invariant T: CWhisper runs only the graphs of whisper.cpp for the catalog models (base,
   small-q5_1, tiny-q5_1) and the Silero VAD model. Each tensor of them has fewer than 2^31
   elements and fewer than 2^31 bytes. The largest is the small-q5_1 token embedding, with
   39,832,320 elements.
   - W1 tensor sizes into int locals, 141 sites (T): ops.cpp 128, ggml-cpu.c 4, repack.cpp 4,
     ggml-blas.cpp 3, whisper.cpp 2.
   - W2 index and partition arithmetic, 92 sites (T: each index is below the element count of
     its tensor): ops.cpp 92.
   - W3 shape value to an int parameter, 131 sites (T): ops.cpp 91, ggml-cpu.c 19, repack.cpp 7,
     ggml.c 6, tiled.cpp 3, simd-gemm.h 2, ggml-quants.c 2, whisper.cpp 1.
   - W4 quant blocks of a row, 68 sites (T: the count is the element count of one row): cpu
     repack.cpp 34, ggml-quants.c 26, and 2 each in arch/arm/quants.c, arch/arm/repack.cpp,
     arch/x86/quants.c, and arch/x86/repack.cpp.
   - W5 byte strides and offsets, 22 sites (T in bytes): ops.cpp 14, ggml.c 8. Two of the ggml.c
     sites store strides in the int32 op params of ggml_acc and ggml_set, the upstream format.
   - W6 container sizes, 44 sites (a bound per container: at most 448 tokens, a vocabulary of
     51,865, at most 100 languages, at most 9,600,000 samples in a piece of 10 min, at most 2
     backends, a path under PATH_MAX): whisper.cpp 34, ggml-backend-meta.cpp 6, ggml-impl.h 2,
     ggml-backend-reg.cpp 1, ggml.c 1.
   - W7 thread and task counts, 3 sites (at most n_threads): ggml-cpu.c 3.
   - W8 local value ranges, 18 sites (a local bound at each site, for example a ternary quant
     value of 0 to 2, an index inside one block, or an hparam that the model file stores as
     int32): whisper.cpp 5, ggml-quants.c 4, arch/arm/repack.cpp 3, ops.cpp 2, ggml.c 2,
     ggml-opt.cpp 1, gguf.cpp 1.
   - W9 expert counts of MUL_MAT_ID, 7 sites (T; whisper builds no MUL_MAT_ID): ggml-cpu.c 4,
     repack.cpp 3.
   - W10 head counts as uint32, 4 sites (T: at most 12 heads): ops.cpp 4.
2. Macro text (25 -Wambiguous-macro sites on each arch). SwiftPM builds C with clang modules, so
   the SDK macros and the ggml macros are both visible. MIN and MAX in ggml-impl.h, and the
   unguarded MAX of ggml-alloc.c, get the token text of the SDK macros. static_assert in
   ggml-impl.h and ggml-common.h is defined as _Static_assert, the SDK text. Same expansion.
3. Pragmas: the 5 "#pragma GCC diagnostic" lines that ignore a warning, in amx/mmq.cpp (-Wpedantic,
   -Wunused-local-typedefs) and in the three repack.cpp files (-Woverlength-strings) are
   removed. The build enables none of these warnings, so the strict build proves that they hide
   nothing.
4. No code path loads a library or starts a program from an environment variable:
   - src/whisper.cpp: the ANEForge encoder is removed: the environment read and the init call in
     whisper_init_state, the encode branch in whisper_encode_internal (the other branch stays),
     and the free call in whisper_free_state. Package.swift excludes
     src/aneforge/whisper-aneforge.cpp.
   - ggml/src/ggml-backend-reg.cpp: ggml_backend_load_all_from_path no longer reads a backend
     path from the environment.
   - ggml/src/ggml.c: on Apple, ggml_print_backtrace prints the native backtrace
     (ggml_print_backtrace_symbols) and returns. The environment read and its two warning lines
     are removed, and the fork and exec of gdb or lldb are under #if !defined(__APPLE__).
5. Abort checks, in src/whisper.cpp: whisper_full passes its abort_callback to the scheduler
   overload of ggml_graph_compute_helper for the encoder, the cross, and the decoder graphs.
   The VAD graph gets no callback, and the VAD window loop checks the callback every 32
   windows. The mel frame loop checks it every 32 frames of thread 0, and get_signal_energy
   every 65,536 samples. Without these checks a stop waits for the running 30 s window.

To update whisper.cpp: copy the same files from the new tarball. Apply the casts again: the
clang source ranges of the warnings (-fdiagnostics-print-source-range-info) give the expression
of each site, and each new site needs a group with an invariant. Apply changes 2 to 5 again.
Check the define list of Package.swift against ggml/src/CMakeLists.txt. Build with
`make build`, `swift build --arch arm64`, and `make app`: each build must give zero warnings.
